      "date_raw": "Fri, 14 May 2021 14:02:07 -0400",
      "body": "Hi,\nAs pointed out to me by Dr. Christina Bergonzo, G-U base pairing can\nbe very transient, so you may want to try adding the 'allframes'\nkeyword to the 'nastruct' command so that cpptraj determines base\npairing each frame instead of based on the first frame.\n-Dan\nOn Thu, May 13, 2021 at 6:49 PM Francis Acquah\n<francis.asieduacquah.outlook.com> wrote:\n>\n> Hello all,\n> I am trying to use the nastruct command to calculate the basic nucleic acids structure parameters of 500 frame MD simulation of a 32bp RNA.\n> The RNA has 3 consecutive G-U base pairs (2 of them; r10 - r13 & 20 - 22)\n>\n> However the:\n> BP.data output\n> BPstep.data output\n> Helix.data output\n>\n> all do not capture parameters for the G-U bps. They are missing from all the output files.\n>\n> For example::::\n>\n> %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n>\n> BP.data output>>>>\n> #Frame Base1 Base2 Shear Stretch Stagger Buckle Propeller Opening BP HB Major Minor\n> 1 1 64 -0.4832 -0.1082 -0.9687 -15.6349 -10.2136 6.3749 1 2 0.0000 12.8730\n> 1 3 62 0.0638 -0.2095 -0.4135 1.3191 -13.8867 0.2925 1 2 18.6218 13.2438\n> 1 4 61 -2.2295 -0.4624 -0.7918 -8.9326 -8.1879 0.5222 1 0 18.8094 13.1070\n> 1 5 60 -0.3302 -0.2089 -0.6546 2.7610 -18.5153 3.1471 1 2 18.1348 13.2356\n> 1 6 59 -0.3048 -0.2837 -0.3637 -8.9297 -26.2722 -3.6968 1 2 18.0371 13.3502\n> 1 8 57 0.3137 0.2243 -0.0599 -6.5792 -19.9784 -1.2544 1 2 18.5768 13.6837\n> 1 9 56 -0.5400 -0.2885 -0.5400 -7.2689 -27.7735 5.3289 1 2 19.2228 13.1121\n> 1 10 55 -0.6456 -0.1005 0.0359 -0.3315 -12.2037 1.4471 1 2 18.7792 13.1521\n> 1 14 51 -0.2762 -0.0595 -0.5191 7.6241 -12.9440 5.3462 1 2 17.8080 12.9903\n> 1 15 50 -0.3271 -0.0187 -0.0433 6.1429 -9.8041 -1.4565 1 2 18.7425 13.3373\n> 1 16 49 -0.4485 0.0501 0.2836 0.5355 -26.4200 0.3466 1 2 18.6483 13.4823\n> 1 17 48 0.3290 -0.0690 -0.2244 12.0882 -12.8594 -8.0159 1 2 19.0141 13.5715\n> 1 18 47 -0.